# Trinity Muon Simulation - CORSIKA 8 chain (v2.0)

This directory (`Muon_Trinity/cluster_corsika8_2.0/`) drives the Trinity muon
simulation chain:

    CORSIKA 8 Cherenkov generation -> particle-location correction
      -> Trinity container chain (CIO -> GrOptics -> CARE) -> CSV summaries

It has two layers:

1. **Adaptive trigger-region scan** (self-resubmitting): `adaptive_controller.py`
   + `submit_adaptive_scan.sh`. It explores `(zenith, azimuth, production
   height)` intelligently (N-doubling per cell) and stops when a shell yields no
   triggers. See `README_adaptive_scan.md`.
2. **Per-event chain**:
   `base_muon_event_generation/run_corsika8_trinity_chain_tree.slurm`.
   See `base_muon_event_generation/README.md`.

## Magnetic-field muon correction

The scan angles `(zenith, azimuth)` are the **expected arrival** angles of the
muon at the detector plane, not the injection angles. For every
`(zenith, azimuth, height)` cell the controller calls
`magnetic_field_muon_correction.back_track_muon` to predict the **injection**
position and direction that brings the muon to the telescope (an exact
constant-field helix in a curved atmosphere). The prediction is passed to
CORSIKA 8 and stored in `metadata.yaml`. `back_track_muon` also returns a
`survival_probability` (muon decay over the back-tracked path), used to skip
cells below `--min-survival-probability` (shipped default **0.5**; the
controller's own argparse default is `0.1`). Skipped cells submit no jobs and
contribute no triggers, so a shell whose cells are all skipped ends the scan for
that energy — see `README_adaptive_scan.md` §15.

The telescope can still be relocated as a fallback
(`--telescope-position-correction 1` + `particle_location_correction.py
--recenter`); the recentered offset is stored in the CSV
(`correction_x_m`/`correction_y_m`).

## Output tree

```
<OUTPUT_BASE_DIR>/pdg{PDG}_E{ENERGY}_r{TEL_RADIUS}_s{SEED}/
  zen{ZENITH}/            # EXPECTED arrival zenith (scan input)
    az{AZIMUTH}/          # EXPECTED arrival azimuth (scan input)
      h{INJ_HEIGHT}/      # production height (m)
        x{TEL_X}_y{TEL_Y}_z{TEL_Z}/
          CORSIKA8/         # cherenkov_hits.dat (+ cherenkov_hits_base.dat)
          CIO/              # cherenkov_hits.cph (GrOptics input)
          GROPT/            # telescope response
          CARE/             # camera response (cherenkov_hits.root)
          metadata.yaml
          correction_report_firstpass.json
```

`OUTPUT_BASE_DIR` for the adaptive scan is
`/scratch/general/vast/u1520754/muon_sim_chain_tree_adaptive`.

Note: the height level no longer carries injection offsets. Pre-existing
`h<number>_ix*_iy*` directories are migrated with
`migrate_tree_remove_injection.sh <BASE_PATH> --apply`.

## Quick start

```bash
bash $HOME/Muon_Trinity/cluster_corsika8_2.0/submit_adaptive_scan.sh \
    --energy 1e3 \
    --az-values 261,262,263,270,271,272,273 \
    --min-survival-probability 0.1
```

Any energy string is accepted (`--energy 1e3`, `--energy 4466.84`, ...). Any option
passed here **overrides** the corresponding `adaptive_defaults` value — the shipped
defaults use 7 azimuths and `min_survival_probability = 0.5`, so the command above
runs a narrower azimuth list with a looser survival cut. See
`README_adaptive_scan.md` §5.3 (what each shipped default actually does) and §15
(operating envelope and traps); sections 1-3 and 14 cover the general design.

## File map

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `adaptive_controller.py` | Adaptive-scan state machine + magnetic correction |
| `magnetic_field_muon_correction.py` | `back_track_muon`: arrival -> injection + survival |
| `submit_adaptive_scan.sh` | Launcher for the adaptive scan |
| `Trinity_adaptive_input.py` | Generates the input JSON (defaults + energy list) |
| `particle_location_correction.py` | Eventio correction / filtering / recentering |
| `base_muon_event_generation/` | Per-event Slurm chain |
| `save_data2csv/` | CARE -> CSV workers |
| `migrate_tree_remove_injection.sh` | One-off tree migration (strip `_ix*_iy*`) |
